    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839e9f443598019f4dbb219619b9&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "ASN Chairperson - Cresson",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: ASN Chairperson - Cresson Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 227 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \"Great College to Work For,” invites applications from highly qualified individuals to join our leadership team in the School of Nursing as the ASN Chairperson beginning August 2026/Fall 2026 in Cresson, PA. Current Opening Reporting to the Dean of Nursing, the ASN Chairperson provides departmental oversight and clinical coordination of the College’s Associate of Science in Nursing program, based in Cresson, PA.  This position is responsible to ensure that the ASN program’s curriculum and outcomes align with the guidelines of Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and the PA State Board of Nursing.  This includes modeling good instruction, including integration of technology, development of quality course syllabi, establishing policy and procedures within the program, and assisting others within the ASN program with these matters. This position also holds teaching responsibilities within the ASN program. This position requires a regular, full-time 10-month appointment from August – May, with additional required workdays during the summer at the beginning and end of the core academic year.  The ASN Chairperson is responsible for a workload of 24 credits or equivalent, which includes a 21-credit release for administrative duties, per academic year, and supervises all full-time and part-time faculty assigned to the ASN Program. Faculty are expected to have a regular presence on campus (5 days per week required) to engage with students both inside and outside of the classroom. In addition to teaching, the ASN Chairperson is responsible to lead departmental initiatives, recruit and mentor adjunct faculty, and assure courses are properly resourced with appropriate academic quality and rigor.  Also participates in department meetings, committee work, advises students academically, holds regular office hours, and assists with College events, service to the College, and other activities. Mount Aloysius College offers a generous benefits package for full-time employees including but not limited to: medical/health, dental, vision, and life insurance; short-term and long-term disability insurance; Retirement plan match; tuition remission; and an employee assistance program, among others. Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) required.  Doctorate preferred (PhD, DNP, EdD) earned or in final semester/ABD with pending graduation date.  Two (2) to three (3) years of leadership experience in nursing education administration required.  Prior classroom and clinical teaching experience at the collegiate level required. Valid, unencumbered license as a registered nurse or advanced practice nurse in Pennsylvania required. Minimum 3-4 years of nursing experience and a demonstrated ability to perform at a high level is required. A strong student focus is required, with the ability to relay information effectively.  Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected.  Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and demonstrate the ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. Proficiency in curriculum design, evaluation, instruction, program administration, and academic advising also preferred.  Faculty rank is dependent upon education, experience and credentials. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College ( www.mtaloy.edu ) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania’s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. The School of Nursing and Health Sciences offers a real-world experience for nursing students on site at Mount Aloysius College.  Our facilities include a four-room simulation nursing unit, interactive manikins and realistic hospital systems (including a state-of-the-art anatomage table).  Built-in observation units, modern study and lounge areas create inviting study spaces for students and support a personalized learning experience for each student.  Additionally, we are thrilled to offer an unprecedented opportunity for future nurses through the Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship, in partnership with UPMC Altoona, Bedford & Somerset.  To learn more about our nursing program and the Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship, please follow the links below: Nursing Program Overview - Mount Aloysius College Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship Initiative in affiliation with UPMC - Mount Aloysius College Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  All applicants should submit a resume with accompanying cover letter via the Mount Aloysius College website at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities/. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a068ae6d3432f9&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Medical Terminology",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Adjunct Faculty - Medical Terminology Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 231 # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Faculty – Medical Terminology (Cresson) Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a “Great College to Work For,” is searching for qualified candidates to teach undergraduate Medical Terminology coursework on an adjunct basis during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.  Opportunities exist in multiple content areas. Each 15-week course is scheduled to be taught in person at our Cresson location during daytime hours.  Sections will be offered twice a week, Monday/Wednesday or Tuesday/Thursday, depending on need. Faculty are expected to create an interactive, student-centered learning environment in the classroom.  Some basic course materials should be made available to students using the Canvas Learning Management System. Adjunct faculty at Mount Aloysius College may participate in our retirement savings plan, and are eligible for limited tuition remission benefits for themselves and their dependents.  As an Adjunct faculty member, you also receive complimentary access to our wellness center/gym, are eligible for the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and have access to various employee discounts. Qualifications Master’s degree or graduate degree in a related field such as Nursing, Public Health, Health Sciences, Physician Assistant Studies, Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy or other related field, and at least two (2) years of relevant classroom teaching experience is required.  Collegiate teaching experience is highly preferred.  An equivalent combination of applicable teaching experience and education will be considered.  Experience using Canvas Learning Management System, or similar LMS preferred.  Must have the ability to remain flexible, employ a range of teaching methods, and effectively incorporate technology into the teaching/learning process.  Strong interpersonal and both oral and written communication skills, organizational and record-keeping skills necessary. Adjunct appointments are single-semester opportunities only, with no guarantee of future appointments. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania’s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references in confidence to the Office of Human Resources via their online application.  Review of applications will begin immediately and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 814-886-6494. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
