      "title": "Administrative Coordinator - DuBois",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Administrative Coordinator - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 233 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a “Great College to Work For,” seeks a highly skilled and organized individual to serve as the Administrative Coordinator for Nursing, Surgical Technology, and Medical Imaging programs, beginning August 2026/Fall 2026 in DuBois, PA. Current Opening The Administrative Coordinator is responsible for a variety of high-level clerical and administrative duties to support the Nursing, Surg-Tech, and Medical Imaging teams in DuBois and to ensure consistent and efficient operations in all DuBois programs. This role requires significant coordination responsibilities and the ability to accurately track and organize a variety of data for compliance and reporting purposes using Excel and/or Google Sheets.  Also prepares signature-ready letters, revises handbooks and other procedural documents as assigned. The Administrative Coordinator communicates and corresponds regularly with clinical sites and agency partners.  Also assists with planning and coordination of special events and programs.  Maintains confidential files across all DuBois programs, including management of demographic information and ensures that all required student and faculty documentation/licensure is current and accurately filed. This position also assists with departmental website updates, gathers and organizes documentation for the academic appeals process, directs callers and visitors as appropriate, schedules meetings, and disseminates mail.  Also responsible to enter budget requests, submit purchase requisitions, and place supply orders. May interview prospective work-study students, and provide supervision to assigned students. This is a full-time, year-round, benefit-eligible position. While some flexibility in scheduling exists, this position is on campus in DuBois, PA (5 days per week required), and is not eligible for remote work. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two (2) years of experience in executive or high-level administrative support roles required. Previous experience working in a secondary or post-secondary education setting is preferred. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Above average verbal, written, interpersonal and organizational skills required; Proficiency in Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite, and AdobeSign required. Advanced skills in Microsoft Word and Excel desired.  Demonstrated ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office with little to no supervision is required.  The successful candidate must be able to work collaboratively with others and exercise independent thinking.  Should be able to foresee risks and anticipate needs, and make sound decisions.  Ability to quickly and efficiently learn software that is highly utilized within the Higher Education space required.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College’s Expansion into DuBois, PA Mount Aloysius College is bringing nursing education to DuBois beginning Fall 2026!  Students can complete pre-nursing coursework this fall, and begin their path toward a rewarding healthcare career close to home with a two year associates degree. Through a new collaboration with Penn Highlands Healthcare, eligible nursing students may receive up to $48,000 in combined financial support, along with hands-on clinical opportunities and pathways to employment after graduation. Students can also apply for our radiography and surgical technology programs in DuBois, both of which are also in partnership with Penn Highlands Healthcare. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.  All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
