      "title": "Administrative Coordinator - School of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Administrative Coordinator - School of Health Sciences Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 248 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a “Great College to Work For,” invites applications for a full-time Administrative Coordinator for the School of Health Sciences.  This position  provides direct administrative support to the Dean of the School of Business, Arts, and Sciences & Health Sciences, as well as additional support for Department Chairs, Clinical Coordinators, and Division Faculty. In the Administrative Coordinator capacity, the successful candidate serves as the main point of contact for all programs within the School of Health Sciences, which include Medical Imaging and Radiological Sciences, Physical Therapist Assistant, Science and Mathematics, Surgical Technology, and Ultrasonography.  The Administrative Coordinator receives telephone, email, and in-person inquiries and directs callers/visitors as appropriate.  Responsible for the preparation of correspondence, reports, and other documents, including official student notices, meeting minutes, programmatic accreditation preparation, etc.  Responsible for accurate data coordination and data entry for the School of Health Sciences; maintains electronic records of important documents in a neat and organized manner.  Coordinates timely management, completion and renewal of affiliation agreements with local healthcare organizations and other agencies; schedules meetings as directed; proctors make-up and licensing exams on an as-needed basis. The Administrative Coordinator also assists with preparation and implementation of various events hosted by the School of Health Sciences each year. Also, in this position, the successful candidate supports the Medical Imaging and Ultrasonography departments and their respective clinical coordinators in the clinical placement of students.  To fulfill this responsibility, the Coordinator conducts outreach with existing and potential partners to provide clinical experiences for students, facilitates the acquisition of Clinical Education Agreements, prepares and delivers placement letters and reports, and maintains current and well-organized documentation.  The Coordinator also manages the health screening process for students’ placement in required clinical rotations in the Medical Imaging and Ultrasonography departments.  To meet this requirement, the Coordinator ensures student health screenings are complete and up-to-date, verifies that records are uploaded in a timely manner, maintains detailed records of facility requirements, and manages dosimeters for the Medical Imaging department. Qualifications Associate Degree in secretarial/office administration or equivalent required.  Three (3) years of administrative/secretarial support experience required.  Professional work experience in the higher education setting is a plus.  A strong customer service focus is required, with the ability to effectively relay information via telephone and email communications.  Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected, as well as computer skills, including the ability to learn and effectively utilize the Jenzabar system.  Proficiency in Microsoft Word and Excel required; advanced skill in creating Excel spreadsheets also required.  Must be able to work under minimal supervision and demonstrate ability to prioritize, develop and manage workflow processes, and complete responsibilities in an organized and timely manner.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This is a full-time, 12-month, benefit-eligible position. While some flexibility in scheduling and the opportunity for periodic remote days exists, this position is on campus in Cresson, PA, and is not eligible for remote work. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania’s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.  All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.  Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a11bda7ff22187&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 245 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a “Great College to Work For,” invites applications to join our Advancement & Engagement team as a full-time, year-round Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations. The Director of Annual Giving and Alumni Relations provides strategic leadership for the College’s annual giving and alumni engagement programs, with responsibility for building lifelong relationships between Mount Aloysius College and its alumni, parents, families, friends, and other members of the College Community. This position develops and executes comprehensive annual giving strategies designed to increase donor acquisition, participation, retention, and philanthropic support.  The Director leads alumni engagement initiatives that strengthen connections to the College and create meaningful opportunities for alumni to remain involved, informed, and invested in the institution. Working collaboratively across the Advancement and Engagement Department, the Director will use data, personal engagement, digital and traditional communications, events, and volunteer leadership to develop a sustainable pipeline of donors and advocates.  The position will also identify opportunities to transition annual donors and engaged alumni into deeper philanthropic relationships with the College. The Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations is a non-voting ex-officio member of the Alumni Association Executive Board of Directors; and provides leadership and support to the Alumni Association in collaboration with the Executive Board. Advancement & Engagement at Mount Aloysius College is a comprehensive advancement services enterprise comprised of development/fundraising, alumni relations, grant writing & research, and related communications and events.  Our team’s mission is to build strong, lifelong relationships with Mount Aloysius College's constituents, match donors' interests with College’s needs and priorities, and secure the financial resources necessary to support the Mission of the College. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred.  Five (5) to seven (7) years of progressively responsible administrative experience leading teams and managing complex projects or events required.  Experience in higher education, fundraising, and working with volunteers is a plus.  Excellent verbal, written, interpersonal, organizational, and listening skills required, and the ability to build and foster relationships across a diverse spectrum of individuals is a must.  Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite required. Experience with Raiser’s Edge database is a plus.  Periodic work on evenings and weekends is required.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania’s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.  All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.  Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
