    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78859fa152cc4201a1697834b46eeb&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "FWS - Residence Life - Fall",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Residence Life - Fall Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 569 # of Openings: 1 The Federal Work-Study assigned to Residence Life will primarily act as a support to the Residence Life administrative team. The Residence Life assistant will be responsible for a variety of projects such as creating bulletin boards, organizing and administering intramural sports, replacing RA duty signs and helping to report general information of the halls. As a representative of Residence Life, they should be kind and ready to engage with the student body.  They must also be a student of upstanding character, as they will be trusted  with access to each of the Residence halls on campus. Residence Life Assistants are supervised by Residence Life Pro Staff. FWS Residence Life Assistant Responsibilities: Replace RA on duty signs Create bulletin boards for the Residence Life Office Organize and execute Intramural Sports Assist with departmental administrative tasks Bring any known concerns to Residence Life Pro Staff Help with departmental organization Assist with programming efforts when needed Additional jobs as assigned by Residence Life Pro Staff Contact Information Kristyan Hahn - khahn@mtaloy.edu, (814) 886-6388 Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct 