      "title": "FWS - Student Activities - SPRING",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Student Activities - SPRING Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 258 # of Openings: 11 Assistant will supervise the recreational, cardiovascular, and physical fitness areas of the student union. Assistant will be responsible for monitoring persons using these areas during building hours of operation, distributing recreational and physical fitness equipment as necessary, and assisting with special events sponsored by OSA, Student Affairs, and/or the College. Other projects, mostly creative, will be assigned on an as needed basis by the Director of Student Activities to be accomplished while working at the Fitness Center desk. Hours include weekends and evenings. Resident students are preferred, but any student with a flexible schedule can apply. Contact Information Cari Crago - ccrago@mtaloy.edu Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea15447f701a16955b3a36651&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Admissions Counselor Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 281 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a “Great College to Work For,” seeks highly motivated individuals with experience in K-12 or higher education to serve as a full-time Admissions Counselor, responsible for recruiting students in an assigned geographical territory. Current Opening The Admissions Counselor is responsible to cultivate interest from prospective students in attending Mount Aloysius, with a primary focus on recruiting high school students within an assigned geographic territory whose academic interests and goals align with the College’s offerings.  The Admissions Counselor creates and implements recruitment and outreach plans for assigned areas; coordinates comprehensive plans for travel, and conducts outreach to recruit a diverse and talented pool of student applicants.  The Admissions Counselor also provides personalized, consistent communication to prospective students through multiple channels and delivers frequent presentations to small groups to promote the College’s educational opportunities and campus community. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required.  Experience working in a collegiate Admissions office is strongly preferred. Valid driver’s license required.  Position requires frequent travel, overnight trips and ability to interact regularly with students and other stakeholders both in person and through virtual platforms.  Experience working with high school-aged students is a plus. Excellent verbal, written, interpersonal, organizational, and listening skills required.  Ability to remain patient and professional, particularly when navigating complex situations, is required.  Demonstrated ability to prioritize, multitask, meet deadlines, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office required.  Must be able to work independently as well as collaborate effectively with team members.  Proficiency in Google Suite and Microsoft Office Suite required. Advanced skills in Microsoft Word and Excel desired.  Ability to quickly and efficiently learn software that is highly utilized within the Admissions space (Slate, Jenzabar, etc.) required.  Prior experience with these systems is a plus.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. Occasional weekend and evening hours are required on an as needed basis. This is a full-time, 12-month benefit eligible position.  While some flexibility in scheduling and the opportunity for periodic remote days exists, this position is on campus in Cresson, PA and is not eligible for remote work. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania’s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds – diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.  All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.  Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea15447f701a17eec17076a05&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "FWS - Theatre Production Assistant - Spring",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Theatre Production Assistant - Spring Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 576 # of Openings: 1 The Production Assistant will help to maintain the production spaces for the theatre department. Duties will include cleaning and organizing the scenic and costume areas, pulling costumes and props, building scenery and costumes, repairing any pieces needed for the current production. The individual should have a working knowledge of the theatre as well as an understanding of stagecraft and costuming. Contact Information Ben Roberts - (814) 886-6409 Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea15447f701a17eed0dce6a9a&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "FWS - Theatre - Spring",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Theatre - Spring Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 577 # of Openings: 1 Office assistant will assist with mailings, filing, and maintaining databases as they related to the theatre department. They may also be called to assist with production needs such as running posters, assisting with costumes and/or scenery construction and helping with stage properties. The individual needs to be dependable and have a working knowledge of the theatre, is preferred. Contact Information Ben Roberts - (814) 886-6409 Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea15447f701a17eef325c6bc2&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "FWS - Mission & Ministry - Spring",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Mission & Ministry - Spring Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 578 # of Openings: 3 In all aspects of performance, during scheduled work time and outside of it, an Office Assistant is an ambassador for the Office of Mission & Ministry. The Office Assistant must have some basic computer knowledge, filing skills, and willingness to do a variety of tasks. Dependability, organization and confidentiality are required.  Mission & Ministry appreciates assistance with any or all of the following tasks: clerical work, including filing, Xeroxing, minor on-campus errands, creating and posting program advertisements throughout campus, maintaining Mission & Ministry bulletin boards. Assistants may also be called upon to be present for on-campus programs sponsored by Mission & Ministry and aid with program preparation. Other duties will include assisting with Chapel tasks such as changing missalettes and filing music. It is helpful if the student could be available on a flexible schedule, but it is not required. Contact Information Andre McCarville - 814-886-6483 - amccarville@mtaloy.edu Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7887a1a150293901a16936004e64be&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "FWS - Financial Aid Office - FALL",
      "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: FWS - Financial Aid Office - FALL Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 274 # of Openings: 1 Student is primarily responsible for the creation of all student files, maintenance of entire filing system and the distribution of paperwork to those files. In addition, File Maintenance Clerk will also help with general office duties including mailings, alphabetizing of paperwork, etc. Contact Information Katlyn Poet - 814-886-6496, kpoet@mtaloy.edu Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"
    }
